{"name":"Spotlight","hex":"#faeacd","fetched":"2026-10-16","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"spotlight","whole":true,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A bright, directional light or lamp, especially one used to illuminate the focus or center of attention on a stage.","The circle of light shed by a spotlight."]},{"part":"Verb","definitions":["To illuminate with a spotlight.","To draw attention to."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/spotlight"}],"entries":[{"title":"Spotlight (theatre lighting)","blocks":[{"text":"A spotlight is a powerful stage lighting instrument which projects a bright beam of light onto a performance space. Spotlights are controlled by a spotlight operator who tracks actors around the stage. Spotlights are most commonly used in concerts, musicals and large-scale presentations in which highlighting a specific mobile individual is critical. Spotlights are sometimes located overhead on catwalks. In some theatres, they may also be located in the control booth or purpose-built \"spot booths\" in addition to the catwalk."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/David_%26_Kim_%282010-09-17_by_Ian_T._McFarland%29.jpg/330px-David_%26_Kim_%282010-09-17_by_Ian_T._McFarland%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spotlight_(theatre_lighting)","wikidata":"Q82916"},{"title":"Spotlight (film)","blocks":[{"text":"Spotlight is a 2015 American biographical drama film directed by Tom McCarthy and written by McCarthy and Josh Singer. The film follows The Boston Globe's \"Spotlight\" team, the oldest continuously operating newspaper investigative journalist unit in the United States, and its investigation into a decades-long coverup of widespread and systemic child sex abuse by numerous priests of the Roman Catholic Archdiocese of Boston. Although the plot was original, it is based on a series of stories by the Spotlight team that earned The Globe the 2003 Pulitzer Prize for Public Service. The film features an ensemble cast including Mark Ruffalo, Michael Keaton, Rachel McAdams, John Slattery, Stanley Tucci, Brian d'Arcy James, Liev Schreiber, and Billy Crudup."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/en/f/f3/Spotlight_%28film%29_poster.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Spotlight_(film)","wikidata":"Q18154496"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/David_%26_Kim_%282010-09-17_by_Ian_T._McFarland%29.jpg/500px-David_%26_Kim_%282010-09-17_by_Ian_T._McFarland%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/David_%26_Kim_%282010-09-17_by_Ian_T._McFarland%29.jpg/1280px-David_%26_Kim_%282010-09-17_by_Ian_T._McFarland%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/f/f5/David_%26_Kim_%282010-09-17_by_Ian_T._McFarland%29.jpg/500px-David_%26_Kim_%282010-09-17_by_Ian_T._McFarland%29.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"Spotlights in use at a music performance","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3ADavid_%26_Kim_(2010-09-17_by_Ian_T._McFarland).jpg"},{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Follow_Spot.jpg/500px-Follow_Spot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 1x, https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Follow_Spot.jpg/1280px-Follow_Spot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail 2x","src":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/0/07/Follow_Spot.jpg/500px-Follow_Spot.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=parser&utm_content=thumbnail","alt":"A spotlight","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/File%3AFollow_Spot.jpg"},{"srcset":"https://